Spec 036, flake-proof gates: the gate's part, for the Author's hand (tools/gates/** is human-only).
Branch feat/036-flake-proof-gates; built from refs/heads/main at 42019d3d8cd1 (plain copies, diff -u).
What it does: when make test fails, the test step reruns exactly its failed tests once, in make test's own
container, and names them "flaky:" in its line and the summary line when they pass; a branch that changes only
notes and records no code names skips test, evals, redteam, matrix-h, and image ("docs-only: N files") and checks
its links alone. Tests first in tools/gates/test/test_gate.py. See the note:
docs/merge-requests/2026-11-23-feat-036-flake-proof-gates.md.
Apply from main's checkout, on a branch: patch -p1 < docs/merge-requests/human-patches/2026-11-23-036-gate.patch

